{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"notification-center","name":"Notification Center","version":"0.1.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":[],"author":"mclaudiopt","description":"Queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners through a small companion web app. Talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099.","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Notifications"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Notification Center\n\n> **This Shard does nothing on its own: it needs the companion web app on the TV.** The app (an unsigned `.wgt`, id `NotifCtr01.NotifCenter`)\n> is not part of the catalog. Get it from https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center/releases, sign it with your own certificate and\n> install it (see \"Install the companion app\" below). Without it, `notify` queues messages but nothing is shown.\n\nAny device on your LAN (PC, phone, script) can `POST` a message to this Shard. It queues the message, asks Vetro to\nlaunch the companion app, and the app shows it as a **native Samsung TV banner** (top-right, with the OK /\n\"View history\" buttons, kept in the TV's own notification history). Everything runs on the TV, no PC is needed afterwards.\n\n> **Status: early.** It works end to end on one TV (see \"Tested on\"), but it is **not** a banner on top of the running\n> app: the companion app has to come to the foreground for a few seconds. Read \"Limitations\" before installing.\n\nThe panel (tab **Notifications**) and the app screen are bilingual (English by default, Portuguese optional: use the EN/PT switch in the panel, or `POST .../api/lang` with `{\"lang\":\"pt\"}`) and use a One UI style look. The banner itself is always the TV's own native one.\n\n## Permissions\n\nNone. It does not use `exec`.\n\n## Network\n\n- **Incoming:** HTTP routes under `/plugins/notification-center/api/` (`notify`, `notifications`, `recent`, `ui`, `nt.js`),\n  open to every device that can reach Vetro, like the rest of Vetro when pairing is off.\n- **Outgoing:** one call, to Vetro itself on `127.0.0.1:8099` (`POST /apps/launch`, body `{\"appId\": \"...\"}`), to start the companion app. At most once every 10 seconds.\n  It talks to no other host and downloads no code.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nOnly the display language (`lang`, `en` or `pt`) is kept in `ctx.config`. The id of the companion app is fixed in the code (`NotifCtr01.NotifCenter`), so no route can point the Shard at another app.\nThe queue (up to 5 active notifications) and the list of the last 20 sent are kept in memory only and are cleared when the Shard stops.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nany device --POST notify--> Shard (queue) --POST /apps/launch--> Vetro launches the companion app\ncompanion app --GET notifications--> Shard      (XHR, or <script> if the TV blocks cross-origin XHR)\ncompanion app --new Notification(title, {body})--> TV banner + TV notification history\ncompanion app stays open ~8 s (it must be on screen for the banner to show), then exits\n```\n\nThe companion app is a **thin loader**: its logic is `nt.js`, served by this Shard, so you can change the logic from the\nVetro panel without reinstalling the app on the TV.\n\n## Install\n\n1. Vetro with root connected. If Vetro keeps restarting, set the TV's **Host PC IP to `127.0.0.1`** (Developer Mode); otherwise\n   it can end up in safe mode (\"Resume plugins\", then restart Vetro).\n2. Install this Shard from the catalog and switch it on.\n3. Build and install the companion app (below) with your own certificate. It needs the privileges `notification` and `internet`.\n4. Send a notification:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"seconds\":30}'\n```\n\n**With pairing on (Vetro's default)** a request from another device goes through Vetro's sign-in like every other route, so a script on the LAN needs\n`Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Pair the script once (the TV shows a 6-digit code), as described in Vetro's `SIGN-IN.md`:\n\n```\ncurl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"scripts\"}' http://<TV-IP>:8099/auth/pair\ncurl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"id\":\"<id>\",\"code\":\"<code>\"}' http://<TV-IP>:8099/auth/confirm   # returns the token\ncurl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\"}'\n```\n\nThe companion app on the TV itself (127.0.0.1) needs no key. With pairing off (Vetro's \"Disable pairing mode\") any device on the LAN can send notifications.\n\nFields: `message` (required, 200 characters), `title` (40), `level` (`info`, `ok`, `warn`, `alert`; colours the card on the app screen and the panel, default `info`), `mode` (`both` default, `banner` = native Samsung banner only, `full` = full-screen card only), `seconds` (5-300, how long it stays in the queue), `open`\n(`false` only queues it, without launching the app). The page of this Shard (tab **Notifications**) has a form for it.\n\n## Install the companion app (required)\n\nDownload the unsigned `.wgt` from the releases of https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center, or build it from the three files below (also in `app/`).\nSign it with your own certificate and install it with Apps2Samsung, TV-Store or Tizen Studio. The app id must stay `NotifCtr01.NotifCenter`.\n\n### Source (copy these three files)\n\n`config.xml`\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<widget xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets\" xmlns:tizen=\"http://tizen.org/ns/widgets\" id=\"http://localhost/notifcenter\" version=\"0.1.0\" viewmodes=\"maximized\">\n  <tizen:application id=\"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" package=\"NotifCtr01\" required_version=\"6.0\"/>\n  <name>Notification Center</name>\n  <icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n  <content src=\"index.html\"/>\n  <access origin=\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\" subdomains=\"false\"/>\n  <feature name=\"http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/internet\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/notification\"/>\n  <tizen:profile name=\"tv-samsung\"/>\n</widget>\n```\n\n`index.html`\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Notification Center</title></head>\n<body style=\"background:#0f1218;color:#e8ecf2;font:28px sans-serif;margin:40px\">\n<div id=\"log\"></div>\n<script src=\"js/app.js\"></script>\n</body></html>\n```\n\n`js/app.js` (the loader)\n\n```js\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASES = [\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\"];\n  var PATH = \"/plugins/notification-center/api/nt.js\";\n  var logEl = document.getElementById(\"log\"), i = 0;\n  function say(t) { var d = document.createElement(\"div\"); d.textContent = t; logEl.appendChild(d); }\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= BASES.length) { say(\"Could not load nt.js from the Shard. Is it running?\"); return; }\n    var s = document.createElement(\"script\");\n    s.src = BASES[i++] + PATH + \"?t=\" + new Date().getTime();\n    s.onerror = function () { say(\"nt.js failed: \" + s.src.split(\"?\")[0]); next(); };\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  })();\n})();\n```\n\nThese three files are also in the `app/` folder next to this README. A ready-made, **unsigned** `.wgt` (with an icon) is attached to\nthe releases of https://github.com/mclaudiopt/tv-notification-center (a catalog Shard can only hold text files, so the `.wgt` and its icon are not here).\nAdd any 512x512 `icon.png`, zip the files as `.wgt`, sign it and install it (Apps2Samsung, TV-Store, Tizen Studio).\n`nt.js` also tries the address it was loaded from. If the app shows \"nt.js failed\" (loopback does not answer on some TVs), build the app with the TV's LAN address too:\nadd the TV's own LAN address to `BASES` in `js/app.js` and `nt.js`, and a matching `<access origin=\"...\">` to `config.xml`.\n\n## Limitations (all measured on a real TV)\n\n- **The app must be in the foreground to post.** The web `Notification` API only works while the web app is on screen\n  (a background web app is suspended and its timers stop). So the companion app comes to the front, posts, stays ~8 s\n  (leaving earlier hides the banner), and exits. You will see it for a moment, and what was playing is interrupted briefly.\n- `tizen.notification` / `StatusNotification` **do not exist** on the TV profile; only the web `Notification` API works.\n- **No banner over the running app without launching an app.** I checked that it is not possible from a Shard or a shell:\n  the TV's `libnotification` uses its own sockets (nothing about notifications on the system D-Bus), there is no\n  `notification_test`, and writing to `/opt/dbspace/.notification.db` does not notify the UI. The realistic way is a small\n  background **`service-application`** (native or .NET) with the `notification` privilege calling `NotificationManager.Post`.\n  Nobody has built it here (no Tizen Studio / .NET SDK); **help wanted**.\n- The TV refuses to run **unsigned script files** (\"the file is NOT signed\"); inline commands through Vetro still work. This Shard needs neither.\n- Whether the previous screen comes back cleanly after the app exits was tested only from the launcher, not yet over\n  every kind of source (live TV, HDMI).\n- With pairing off, any device that can reach Vetro's port can send notifications and make Vetro launch the companion app (at most once every 10 s); with pairing on, senders need a key (see above).\n\n## Tested on\n\nSamsung Q70C (TQ55Q70CATXXC), Tizen 9.0, Vetro 0.5.0. The flow (queue, launch, banner top-right, entry in the notification\nhistory, app exits) was tested with an earlier version of this Shard that lived inside another one; this standalone\nversion keeps the same logic and was checked on the TV for its HTTP routes and page.\n","app/config.xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<widget xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets\" xmlns:tizen=\"http://tizen.org/ns/widgets\" id=\"http://localhost/notifcenter\" version=\"0.1.0\" viewmodes=\"maximized\">\n  <tizen:application id=\"NotifCtr01.NotifCenter\" package=\"NotifCtr01\" required_version=\"6.0\"/>\n  <name>Notification Center</name>\n  <icon src=\"icon.png\"/>\n  <content src=\"index.html\"/>\n  <access origin=\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\" subdomains=\"false\"/>\n  <feature name=\"http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/internet\"/>\n  <tizen:privilege name=\"http://tizen.org/privilege/notification\"/>\n  <tizen:profile name=\"tv-samsung\"/>\n</widget>\n","app/index.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Notification Center</title></head>\n<body style=\"background:#0f1218;color:#e8ecf2;font:28px sans-serif;margin:40px\">\n<div id=\"log\"></div>\n<script src=\"js/app.js\"></script>\n</body></html>\n","app/js/app.js":"(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var BASES = [\"http://127.0.0.1:8099\"];\n  var PATH = \"/plugins/notification-center/api/nt.js\";\n  var logEl = document.getElementById(\"log\"), i = 0;\n  function say(t) { var d = document.createElement(\"div\"); d.textContent = t; logEl.appendChild(d); }\n  (function next() {\n    if (i >= BASES.length) { say(\"Could not load nt.js from the Shard. Is it running?\"); return; }\n    var s = document.createElement(\"script\");\n    s.src = BASES[i++] + PATH + \"?t=\" + new Date().getTime();\n    s.onerror = function () { say(\"nt.js failed: \" + s.src.split(\"?\")[0]); next(); };\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  })();\n})();\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Notification Center: queue notifications from any device on the LAN and show them as native TV banners\n// through a small companion web app (see README). It talks only to Vetro on 127.0.0.1:8099 (to launch that app).\n// Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar http = require('http');\n\nvar MAX_TITLE = 40, MAX_MESSAGE = 200, MAX_QUEUE = 5, MAX_RECENT = 20, MAX_BODY = 8192;\nvar DEFAULT_SECONDS = 30, MIN_SECONDS = 5, MAX_SECONDS = 300, OPEN_EVERY_MS = 10000;\nvar DEFAULT_APP = 'NotifCtr01.NotifCenter';\nvar LEVELS = { info: 1, ok: 1, warn: 1, alert: 1 };\nvar MODES = { both: 1, banner: 1, full: 1 };   // banner = native Samsung banner only, full = full-screen card only\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var queue = [];      // active notifications (memory only)\n    var recent = [];     // last ones sent, for the page (memory only)\n    var seq = 0;\n    var lastOpen = 0;\n\n    // Display language of the app screen and the panel: 'en' (default) or 'pt'. The only thing kept in ctx.config.\n    function getLang() { var c = ctx.config.get() || {}; return c.lang === 'pt' ? 'pt' : 'en'; }\n    function appId() { return DEFAULT_APP; }   // fixed: nothing can point the Shard at another app\n    function send(res, code, type, body) {\n        res.writeHead(code, { 'Content-Type': type, 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(body);\n    }\n    function sendJson(res, code, obj) { send(res, code, 'application/json; charset=utf-8', JSON.stringify(obj)); }\n    // The companion app can read the queue as a <script> when the TV's web runtime blocks cross-origin XHR.\n    function sendScript(res, obj) {\n        var json = JSON.stringify(obj).replace(/</g, '\\\\u003c');\n        json = json.split(String.fromCharCode(0x2028)).join('\\\\u2028').split(String.fromCharCode(0x2029)).join('\\\\u2029');\n        send(res, 200, 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8', 'window.__ncNotes&&window.__ncNotes(' + json + ');');\n    }\n    function wantsScript(req) { return /[?&]js=1(&|$)/.test(String(req.url || '')); }\n    function readBody(req, cb) {\n        var s = '';\n        req.on('data', function (d) { s += d; if (s.length > MAX_BODY) { req.destroy(); } });\n        req.on('end', function () { cb(s); });\n    }\n    function clean(text, max) {\n        return String(text == null ? '' : text).replace(/[\\x00-\\x1f]/g, ' ').slice(0, max).trim();\n    }\n    function prune() {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        queue = queue.filter(function (n) { return n.expires > now; });\n    }\n\n    // Asks Vetro to launch the companion app (at most once every 10 s).\n    function openApp() {\n        var now = Date.now();\n        if (now - lastOpen < OPEN_EVERY_MS) { return 'skipped (less than 10 s since the last launch)'; }\n        lastOpen = now;\n        var body = JSON.stringify({ appId: appId() });\n        try {\n            var rq = http.request({\n                host: '127.0.0.1', port: 8099, path: '/apps/launch', method: 'POST', timeout: 5000,\n                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body) }\n            }, function (r) { r.resume(); });\n            rq.on('error', function () { /* Vetro busy or app not installed */ });\n            rq.on('timeout', function () { rq.destroy(); });\n            rq.write(body);\n            rq.end();\n            return 'requested';\n        } catch (e) { return 'error'; }\n    }\n\n    function handleNotify(req, res) {\n        readBody(req, function (raw) {\n            var b;\n            try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n            b = b || {};\n            var message = clean(b.message, MAX_MESSAGE);\n            if (!message) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'message is required' }); }\n            var secs = parseInt(b.seconds, 10);\n            if (!(secs >= MIN_SECONDS)) { secs = DEFAULT_SECONDS; }\n            if (secs > MAX_SECONDS) { secs = MAX_SECONDS; }\n            prune();\n            seq += 1;\n            var note = {\n                id: seq + '-' + Date.now().toString(36),\n                title: clean(b.title, MAX_TITLE),\n                message: message,\n                level: LEVELS[b.level] ? b.level : 'info',\n                mode: MODES[b.mode] ? b.mode : 'both',\n                expires: Date.now() + secs * 1000\n            };\n            queue.push(note);\n            if (queue.length > MAX_QUEUE) { queue.shift(); }\n            recent.unshift({ id: note.id, title: note.title, message: note.message, level: note.level, mode: note.mode, at: Date.now() });\n            if (recent.length > MAX_RECENT) { recent.pop(); }\n            var opened = b.open === false ? 'not requested' : openApp();\n            sendJson(res, 200, { ok: true, id: note.id, open: opened });\n        });\n    }\n\n    function sendFile(res, name, type) {\n        fs.readFile(path.join(__dirname, name), 'utf8', function (err, text) {\n            if (err) { return sendJson(res, 500, { error: name + ' is missing' }); }\n            send(res, 200, type, text);\n        });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {},\n        stop: function () { queue = []; recent = []; },\n        status: function () { prune(); return { queued: queue.length, appId: appId() }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            sub = String(sub || '').split('?')[0].replace(/^\\/+|\\/+$/g, '');\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'ui.html', 'text/html; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'nt.js' && req.method === 'GET') { sendFile(res, 'nt.js', 'application/javascript; charset=utf-8'); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notify' && req.method === 'POST') { handleNotify(req, res); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'notifications' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                prune();\n                var now = Date.now();\n                var out = { lang: getLang(), notifications: queue.map(function (n) {\n                    return { id: n.id, title: n.title, message: n.message, level: n.level, mode: n.mode, seconds: Math.ceil((n.expires - now) / 1000) };\n                }) };\n                if (wantsScript(req)) { sendScript(res, out); } else { sendJson(res, 200, out); }\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'lang' && req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { lang: getLang() }); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'lang' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readBody(req, function (raw) {\n                    var b;\n                    try { b = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'invalid JSON' }); }\n                    if (!b || (b.lang !== 'en' && b.lang !== 'pt')) { return sendJson(res, 400, { error: 'lang must be en or pt' }); }\n                    var c = ctx.config.get() || {};\n                    c.lang = b.lang;\n                    ctx.config.set(c);\n                    sendJson(res, 200, { lang: b.lang });\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'recent' && req.method === 'GET') { sendJson(res, 200, { recent: recent }); return true; }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","nt.js":"// Logic of the companion web app, served by the Shard (the app on the TV is only a thin loader, see README).\n// It runs inside the app, with the app's `notification` privilege. Plain ES5.\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  if (window.__ncLoaded) { return; }\n  window.__ncLoaded = true;\n\n  var BASES = ['http://127.0.0.1:8099'];\n  // Also try the address this script was loaded from (the loader may have reached the Shard over the LAN).\n  try {\n    var me = document.currentScript && document.currentScript.src, o = me && /^(https?:\\/\\/[^\\/]+)\\/plugins\\//.exec(me);\n    if (o && BASES.indexOf(o[1]) < 0) { BASES.push(o[1]); }\n  } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n  var NOTES_PATH = '/plugins/notification-center/api/notifications';\n  var SEEN_KEY = 'nc_seen', STAY_MS = 8000, WATCH_MS = 5000;\n  var logEl = document.getElementById('log');\n  var apiGood = null, busy = false;\n\n\n  // Screen shown while the app is open: a One UI style card (EN/PT by the TV language). The banner itself is the TV's native one.\n  // The language is a Shard setting (default English); it is applied as soon as the first answer from the Shard arrives.\n  var DICT = {\n    en: { wait: 'Notification Center', ready: 'Waiting for notifications', sent: 'Notification sent', back: 'Returning to the previous app in', err: 'Cannot reach the Shard' },\n    pt: { wait: 'Centro de Notifica\\u00E7\\u00F5es', ready: '\\u00C0 espera de avisos', sent: 'Aviso enviado', back: 'A voltar \\u00E0 aplica\\u00E7\\u00E3o anterior em', err: 'Sem liga\\u00E7\\u00E3o ao Shard' }\n  };\n  var TX = DICT.en;\n  var COL = { info: '#2f7bff', ok: '#2fc28b', warn: '#f5a524', alert: '#f0506e' };\n  // One UI style line icons (24x24, round caps): info, done, warning, alert.\n  var ICON_BODY = {\n    info: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 11v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    ok: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M7.6 12.6l3 3 5.8-6.4\"/>',\n    warn: '<path d=\"M12 3.8L21.2 20H2.8z\"/><path d=\"M12 10v4.6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17.4\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    alert: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 7v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"16.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>'\n  };\n  function iconSvg(level, size) {\n    return '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"' + size + '\" height=\"' + size + '\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">' + (ICON_BODY[level] || ICON_BODY.info) + '</svg>';\n  }\n  var cardEl = null;\n  (function buildUi() {\n    var st = document.createElement('style');\n    st.textContent = 'body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 30% 20%,#17203a,#07090f);color:#eef2f9;font-family:SamsungOne,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}' +\n      '#nc{position:fixed;left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);width:1100px;max-width:90%;text-align:center}' +\n      '#nc h1{font-size:44px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 8px}#nc p{font-size:28px;color:#8b96ab;margin:0 0 40px}' +\n      '#nc .card{display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:center;text-align:left;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:36px;padding:34px 42px;border-left:12px solid var(--c);margin-top:24px}' +\n      '#nc .ic{width:96px;height:96px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--c);display:grid;place-items:center;flex:none}' +\n      '#nc .t{font-size:38px;font-weight:600}#nc .m{font-size:30px;color:#c4cde0;margin-top:6px}#log{display:none}';\n    document.head.appendChild(st);\n    cardEl = document.createElement('div'); cardEl.id = 'nc';\n    cardEl.innerHTML = '<h1></h1><p></p><div id=\"ncl\"></div>';\n    document.body.appendChild(cardEl);\n    applyLang('en');\n  })();\n  function applyLang(l) {\n    TX = DICT[l] || DICT.en;\n    if (!cardEl) { return; }\n    cardEl.getElementsByTagName('h1')[0].textContent = '\\uD83D\\uDD14 ' + TX.wait;\n    if (!document.getElementById('ncl').firstChild) { cardEl.getElementsByTagName('p')[0].textContent = TX.ready; }\n  }\n  function showCard(n) {\n    if (!cardEl) { return; }\n    var c = COL[n.level] || COL.info, d = document.createElement('div');\n    d.className = 'card'; d.style.setProperty('--c', c);\n    var ic = document.createElement('div'); ic.className = 'ic'; ic.innerHTML = iconSvg(n.level, 56);\n    var b = document.createElement('div'), t = document.createElement('div'), m = document.createElement('div');\n    t.className = 't'; t.textContent = n.title || ''; m.className = 'm'; m.textContent = n.message || '';\n    b.appendChild(t); b.appendChild(m); d.appendChild(ic); d.appendChild(b);\n    var host = document.getElementById('ncl'); host.appendChild(d);\n    cardEl.getElementsByTagName('p')[0].textContent = TX.sent;\n  }\n\n  function now() { var d = new Date(); function p(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; } return p(d.getHours()) + ':' + p(d.getMinutes()) + ':' + p(d.getSeconds()); }\n  function log(cls, text) {\n    if (!logEl) { return; }\n    var line = document.createElement('div');\n    line.className = cls; line.textContent = now() + '  ' + text;\n    logEl.appendChild(line);\n    while (logEl.childNodes.length > 14) { logEl.removeChild(logEl.firstChild); }\n  }\n\n  function xhrGet(base, cb) {\n    var x = new XMLHttpRequest(), done = false;\n    function end(err, text) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(err, text); } }\n    try {\n      x.open('GET', base + NOTES_PATH); x.timeout = 4000;\n      x.onload = function () { if (x.status === 200) { end(null, x.responseText); } else { end('http ' + x.status); } };\n      x.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n      x.ontimeout = function () { end('timeout'); };\n      x.send();\n    } catch (e) { end('blocked'); }\n  }\n  function scriptGet(base, cb) {\n    var s = document.createElement('script'), done = false, t;\n    function end(err, data) {\n      if (done) { return; }\n      done = true; clearTimeout(t); window.__ncNotes = undefined;\n      if (s.parentNode) { s.parentNode.removeChild(s); }\n      cb(err, data);\n    }\n    window.__ncNotes = function (d) { end(null, d); };\n    s.onerror = function () { end('network'); };\n    t = setTimeout(function () { end('timeout'); }, 5000);\n    s.src = base + NOTES_PATH + '?js=1&t=' + new Date().getTime();\n    (document.head || document.documentElement).appendChild(s);\n  }\n  function fetchQueue(done) {\n    var list = apiGood ? [apiGood] : BASES, i = 0, errors = [];\n    (function next() {\n      if (i >= list.length) { return done(errors.join('; ') || 'no address'); }\n      var base = list[i++];\n      xhrGet(base, function (err, text) {\n        if (!err) { try { apiGood = base; var jd = JSON.parse(text); applyLang(jd.lang); return done(null, jd.notifications || []); } catch (e) { err = 'json'; } }\n        scriptGet(base, function (err2, data) {\n          if (!err2) { apiGood = base; applyLang(data && data.lang); return done(null, (data && data.notifications) || []); }\n          errors.push(base + ' xhr:' + err + ' script:' + err2); next();\n        });\n      });\n    })();\n  }\n\n  function post(title, body, cb) {\n    try {\n      if (!window.Notification) { return cb('window.Notification is missing'); }\n      var show = function () { try { new Notification(title, { body: body }); cb(null); } catch (e) { cb('new Notification: ' + e.message); } };\n      if (Notification.permission === 'granted') { return show(); }\n      var r = Notification.requestPermission(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } });\n      if (r && r.then) { r.then(function (p) { if (p === 'granted') { show(); } else { cb('permission ' + p); } }); }\n    } catch (e) { cb(e.message); }\n  }\n\n  var cdTimer = null;\n  function countdown(sec) {\n    if (!cardEl || cdTimer) { return; }\n    var el = document.createElement('div');\n    el.style.cssText = 'margin-top:48px;color:#8b96ab;font-size:34px';\n    cardEl.appendChild(el);\n    (function tick() {\n      el.innerHTML = '';\n      var lbl = document.createElement('div'), num = document.createElement('div');\n      lbl.textContent = TX.back;\n      num.textContent = String(sec);\n      num.style.cssText = 'font-size:220px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.05;color:#fff';\n      el.appendChild(lbl); el.appendChild(num);\n      if (sec <= 0) { return; }\n      sec -= 1; cdTimer = setTimeout(tick, 1000);\n    })();\n  }\n\n  // On start, on resume and every few seconds while visible: post what is new, stay open while the banner shows, then exit.\n  function check(why) {\n    if (busy) { return; }\n    busy = true;\n    fetchQueue(function (err, list) {\n      if (err) { busy = false; return log('err', why + ': Shard unreachable (' + err + ')'); }\n      var seen = {}; try { seen = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SEEN_KEY) || '{}'); } catch (e) { seen = {}; }\n      var fresh = list.filter(function (n) { return !seen[n.id]; });\n      if (!fresh.length) { busy = false; return log('inf', why + ': nothing new'); }\n      var pending = fresh.length;\n      // mode: 'banner' = native Samsung banner only, 'full' = full-screen card only, anything else = both.\n      var onlyBanner = fresh.every(function (n) { return n.mode === 'banner'; });\n      if (cardEl) { cardEl.style.display = onlyBanner ? 'none' : ''; }\n      fresh.forEach(function (n) {\n        seen[n.id] = 1;\n        if (n.mode !== 'banner') { showCard(n); }\n        (n.mode === 'full' ? function (t, b, cb) { cb(null); } : post)(n.title || 'Notification', n.message || '', function (e) {\n          log(e ? 'err' : 'ok', (n.title || 'Notification') + ': ' + (e || 'posted'));\n          pending -= 1;\n          if (pending) { return; }\n          try { localStorage.setItem(SEEN_KEY, JSON.stringify(seen)); } catch (x) { /* storage unavailable */ }\n          busy = false; countdown(Math.round(STAY_MS / 1000));\n          // Leaving too early hides the banner: stay open while it is on screen.\n          setTimeout(function () { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }, STAY_MS);\n        });\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  check('start');\n  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () { if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') { check('resume'); } });\n  setInterval(function () { if (document.visibilityState !== 'hidden') { check('watch'); } }, WATCH_MS);\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {\n    if (e.keyCode === 10009 || e.keyCode === 27) { try { tizen.application.getCurrentApplication().exit(); } catch (x) { /* not on a TV */ } }\n  });\n})();\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark light\">\n<title>Notification Center</title>\n<style>\n:root { --bg: #0b0e14; --card: #161b26; --line: #262e3f; --txt: #eef2f9; --dim: #8b96ab; --acc: #2f7bff; --info: #2f7bff; --ok: #2fc28b; --warn: #f5a524; --alert: #f0506e; }\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; padding: 16px; font: 15px/1.45 \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--txt); }\n.head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 14px; }\n.logo { width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 12px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2f7bff, #7b5cff); display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 22px; }\nh1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0; flex: 1; font-weight: 600; }\n.lang { display: flex; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; }\n.lang button { border: 0; background: none; color: var(--dim); padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; font: inherit; }\n.lang button.on { background: var(--acc); color: #fff; }\n.grid { display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); }\n.card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; padding: 16px; }\nh2 { font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 12px; font-weight: 600; }\ninput, button { font: inherit; color: inherit; }\ninput[type=text], input[type=number] { width: 100%; background: #0f131c; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\ninput:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--acc); border-color: transparent; }\n.row { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.row label { color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }\n.row input[type=number] { width: 80px; margin: 0; }\n.levels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n.lv { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #0f131c; border-radius: 14px; padding: 10px 4px; cursor: pointer; text-align: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); }\n.lv i { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; margin: 0 auto 6px; }\n.lv.on { color: #fff; border-color: var(--c); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--c); }\n.modes { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n.md { flex: 1; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #0f131c; border-radius: 20px; padding: 8px 6px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--dim); font-size: 12px; }\n.md.on { color: #fff; border-color: var(--acc); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--acc); }\n.rs { margin: 0 0 0 auto; padding: 4px 12px; font-size: 12px; flex: none; }\n.send { margin-left: auto; background: var(--acc); border: 0; border-radius: 22px; padding: 10px 26px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; }\n.send:active { transform: scale(.97); }\n.msg { min-height: 20px; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); } .ok { color: var(--ok); } .err { color: var(--alert); }\n.prev { background: #0f131c; border-radius: 16px; padding: 14px; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; border-left: 5px solid var(--c, var(--info)); }\n.prev .ic { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--c, var(--info)); display: grid; place-items: center; flex: none; }\n.prev b { display: block; } .prev span { color: var(--dim); font-size: 14px; word-break: break-word; }\nul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\nli { display: flex; gap: 10px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); align-items: flex-start; }\nli:last-child { border: 0; }\nli .dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 6px; flex: none; background: var(--c); }\nli small { color: var(--dim); display: block; }\n.ghost { background: none; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; padding: 6px 14px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--dim); margin-top: 10px; }\n.empty { color: var(--dim); text-align: center; padding: 18px 0; }\npre { background: #0f131c; border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px; font-size: 12px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; margin: 0; color: #b9c4dc; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"head\">\n  <div class=\"logo\">&#128276;</div>\n  <h1 data-t=\"title\">Notification Center</h1>\n  <div class=\"lang\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"l-en\">EN</button><button type=\"button\" id=\"l-pt\">PT</button></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"send\">Send a notification</h2>\n    <div class=\"levels\" id=\"levels\"></div>\n    <div class=\"modes\" id=\"modes\"></div>\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"title\" maxlength=\"40\" data-p=\"ph_title\">\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"message\" maxlength=\"200\" data-p=\"ph_msg\">\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <label><span data-t=\"secs\">Seconds</span> <input type=\"number\" id=\"secs\" min=\"5\" max=\"300\" value=\"30\"></label>\n      <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"open\" checked> <span data-t=\"open\">Show on TV now</span></label>\n      <button class=\"send\" id=\"send\" type=\"button\" data-t=\"btn\">Send</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"msg\" id=\"result\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"preview\">Preview</h2>\n    <div class=\"prev\" id=\"prev\"><div class=\"ic\" id=\"pic\"></div><div><b id=\"ptitle\"></b><span id=\"pmsg\"></span></div></div>\n    <div class=\"msg\" data-t=\"prevnote\">The TV shows its own native banner; this is only an approximation.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"recent\">Recently sent</h2>\n    <ul id=\"recent\"></ul>\n    <button class=\"ghost\" id=\"refresh\" type=\"button\" data-t=\"refresh\">Refresh</button>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <h2 data-t=\"app\">Companion app</h2>\n    <div class=\"msg\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px\" data-t=\"appnote\">Launches NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (fixed id). It must be installed on the TV, see the README.</div>\n    <h2 data-t=\"curl\">Send from another device</h2>\n    <pre id=\"curl\"></pre>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };\n  var T = {\n    en: { title: \"Notification Center\", send: \"Send a notification\", secs: \"Seconds\", open: \"Show on TV now\", btn: \"Send\", preview: \"Preview\",\n      prevnote: \"The TV shows its own native banner; this is only an approximation.\", recent: \"Recently sent\", refresh: \"Refresh\", app: \"Companion app\",\n      appnote: \"Launches NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (fixed id). It must be installed on the TV, see the README.\", curl: \"Send from another device\",\n      ph_title: \"Title (optional)\", ph_msg: \"Message\", sending: \"Sending...\", queued: \"Sent to the TV\", queuedq: \"Queued (TV not launched)\", none: \"Nothing sent yet.\", notitle: \"Notification\",\n      info: \"Info\", ok: \"Done\", warn: \"Warning\", alert: \"Alert\", sample: \"Your message appears here\",\n      mode: \"Show as\", m_both: \"Both\", m_banner: \"Samsung banner\", m_full: \"Full screen\", resend: \"Resend\", resent: \"Sent again\" },\n    pt: { title: \"Centro de Notifica\\u00E7\\u00F5es\", send: \"Enviar notifica\\u00E7\\u00E3o\", secs: \"Segundos\", open: \"Mostrar na TV agora\", btn: \"Enviar\", preview: \"Pr\\u00E9-visualiza\\u00E7\\u00E3o\",\n      prevnote: \"A TV mostra o seu pr\\u00F3prio aviso nativo; isto \\u00E9 s\\u00F3 uma aproxima\\u00E7\\u00E3o.\", recent: \"Enviadas recentemente\", refresh: \"Atualizar\", app: \"App companheira\",\n      appnote: \"Lan\\u00E7a NotifCtr01.NotifCenter (id fixo). Tem de estar instalada na TV, ver o README.\", curl: \"Enviar a partir de outro dispositivo\",\n      ph_title: \"T\\u00EDtulo (opcional)\", ph_msg: \"Mensagem\", sending: \"A enviar...\", queued: \"Enviada para a TV\", queuedq: \"Em fila (TV n\\u00E3o lan\\u00E7ada)\", none: \"Ainda nada enviado.\", notitle: \"Notifica\\u00E7\\u00E3o\",\n      info: \"Info\", ok: \"Conclu\\u00EDdo\", warn: \"Aviso\", alert: \"Alerta\", sample: \"A sua mensagem aparece aqui\",\n      mode: \"Mostrar como\", m_both: \"Ambos\", m_banner: \"Aviso Samsung\", m_full: \"Ecr\\u00E3 inteiro\", resend: \"Reenviar\", resent: \"Enviada de novo\" }\n  };\n  var LEVELS = [\"info\", \"ok\", \"warn\", \"alert\"];\n  // One UI style line icons (24x24, round caps): info, done, warning, alert.\n  var ICON_BODY = {\n    info: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 11v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    ok: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M7.6 12.6l3 3 5.8-6.4\"/>',\n    warn: '<path d=\"M12 3.8L21.2 20H2.8z\"/><path d=\"M12 10v4.6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17.4\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>',\n    alert: '<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9.5\"/><path d=\"M12 7v6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"16.6\" r=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/>'\n  };\n  function iconSvg(level, size) {\n    return '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"' + size + '\" height=\"' + size + '\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">' + (ICON_BODY[level] || ICON_BODY.info) + '</svg>';\n  }\n  var COLORS = { info: \"#2f7bff\", ok: \"#2fc28b\", warn: \"#f5a524\", alert: \"#f0506e\" };\n  var lang = \"en\", level = \"info\", mode = \"both\", lastRecent = [];\n  function tr(k) { return T[lang][k] || T.en[k] || k; }\n  function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? \"\" : s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, function (c) { return { \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\", \"'\": \"&#39;\" }[c]; }); }\n  function say(text, cls) { $(\"result\").textContent = text || \"\"; $(\"result\").className = \"msg \" + (cls || \"\"); }\n  function api(path, body) {\n    var opt = body ? { method: \"POST\", headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" }, body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {};\n    return fetch(path, opt).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { if (!r.ok) { throw new Error(j.error || \"error \" + r.status); } return j; }); });\n  }\n  function icon(l) { return iconSvg(l, 24); }\n  function paintLevels() {\n    $(\"levels\").innerHTML = LEVELS.map(function (l) {\n      return '<button type=\"button\" class=\"lv' + (l === level ? \" on\" : \"\") + '\" data-l=\"' + l + '\" style=\"--c:' + COLORS[l] + '\"><i style=\"background:' + COLORS[l] + '\">' + iconSvg(l, 22) + \"</i>\" + esc(tr(l)) + \"</button>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    var b = $(\"levels\").getElementsByTagName(\"button\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < b.length; i++) { b[i].addEventListener(\"click\", function () { level = this.getAttribute(\"data-l\"); paintLevels(); preview(); }); }\n  }\n  function paintModes() {\n    var MODES = [\"both\", \"banner\", \"full\"];\n    $(\"modes\").innerHTML = MODES.map(function (m) {\n      return '<button type=\"button\" class=\"md' + (m === mode ? \" on\" : \"\") + '\" data-m=\"' + m + '\">' + esc(tr(\"m_\" + m)) + \"</button>\";\n    }).join(\"\");\n    var b = $(\"modes\").getElementsByTagName(\"button\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < b.length; i++) { b[i].addEventListener(\"click\", function () { mode = this.getAttribute(\"data-m\"); paintModes(); }); }\n  }\n  function preview() {\n    $(\"prev\").style.setProperty(\"--c\", COLORS[level]);\n    $(\"pic\").innerHTML = icon(level);\n    $(\"ptitle\").textContent = $(\"title\").value || tr(\"notitle\");\n    $(\"pmsg\").textContent = $(\"message\").value || tr(\"sample\");\n  }\n  function recent() {\n    api(\"recent\").then(function (d) {\n      lastRecent = d.recent;\n      $(\"recent\").innerHTML = d.recent.length ? d.recent.map(function (n, i) {\n        return '<li style=\"--c:' + (COLORS[n.level] || COLORS.info) + '\"><span class=\"dot\"></span><div><b>' + esc(n.title || tr(\"notitle\")) + \"</b> \" + esc(n.message) +\n          \"<small>\" + new Date(n.at).toLocaleTimeString() + \"</small></div>\" +\n          '<button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost rs\" data-i=\"' + i + '\">' + esc(tr(\"resend\")) + \"</button></li>\";\n      }).join(\"\") : '<li class=\"empty\">' + esc(tr(\"none\")) + \"</li>\";\n      var rb = $(\"recent\").getElementsByClassName(\"rs\"), k;\n      for (k = 0; k < rb.length; k++) {\n        rb[k].addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n          var n = lastRecent[parseInt(this.getAttribute(\"data-i\"), 10)];\n          if (!n) { return; }\n          api(\"notify\", { title: n.title, message: n.message, level: n.level, mode: n.mode, seconds: parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 30, open: $(\"open\").checked })\n            .then(function () { say(tr(\"resent\"), \"ok\"); recent(); })\n            .catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n        });\n      }\n    }).catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n  }\n  function applyLang() {\n    document.documentElement.lang = lang;\n    var els = document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-t]\"), i;\n    for (i = 0; i < els.length; i++) { els[i].textContent = tr(els[i].getAttribute(\"data-t\")); }\n    els = document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-p]\");\n    for (i = 0; i < els.length; i++) { els[i].placeholder = tr(els[i].getAttribute(\"data-p\")); }\n    $(\"l-en\").className = lang === \"en\" ? \"on\" : \"\"; $(\"l-pt\").className = lang === \"pt\" ? \"on\" : \"\";\n    paintLevels(); paintModes(); preview(); recent();\n  }\n  // The language is a Shard setting (default English); it also decides the language of the app screen on the TV.\n  function setLang(l) { lang = l; applyLang(); api(\"lang\", { lang: l }).catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); }); }\n  // The dashboard frame has no allow-forms: use buttons and the Enter key, not <form>.\n  $(\"send\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    say(tr(\"sending\"));\n    api(\"notify\", { title: $(\"title\").value, message: $(\"message\").value, level: level, mode: mode, seconds: parseInt($(\"secs\").value, 10) || 30, open: $(\"open\").checked })\n      .then(function (r) { say(r.open === \"not requested\" ? tr(\"queuedq\") : tr(\"queued\"), \"ok\"); $(\"message\").value = \"\"; preview(); recent(); })\n      .catch(function (e) { say(e.message, \"err\"); });\n  });\n  $(\"message\").addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) { if (e.key === \"Enter\") { $(\"send\").click(); } });\n  $(\"message\").addEventListener(\"input\", preview); $(\"title\").addEventListener(\"input\", preview);\n  $(\"refresh\").addEventListener(\"click\", recent);\n  $(\"l-en\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () { setLang(\"en\"); });\n  $(\"l-pt\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () { setLang(\"pt\"); });\n  $(\"curl\").textContent = 'curl -X POST http://<TV-IP>:8099/plugins/notification-center/api/notify \\\\\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\\\\n  -d \\'{\"title\":\"Oven\",\"message\":\"Dinner is ready\",\"level\":\"ok\",\"seconds\":30}\\'';\n  applyLang();\n  api(\"lang\").then(function (d) { if (T[d.lang] && d.lang !== lang) { lang = d.lang; applyLang(); } }).catch(function () { /* keep English */ });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}
